VOID R06 force-sensitive physical key array and two-axis potentiometric pointer
* Key cap mechanically compresses individual FSR; EVERY input changes a physical resistance.
* 20meg per R_FSR is a RELEASED-STATE reference, not a force waveform or behavioral model.
* Real selected FSR has >10meg unloaded typically, variable force response; characterize as-built.
* Simultaneous actuation sums through Kirchhoff network; NO character/binary decoder exists.
* Pointer X/Y use two real 10k potentiometers with wipers; 5k/5k is CENTRE reference only.
* An ordinary USB optical mouse/keyboard is NOT directly wired by this passive circuit.
